    {
      "id": "system-smokes",
      "kind": "smoke",
      "scoring": "deterministic",
      "about": "Keyless smokes on a seeded synthetic brain that need a cross-version upgrade, a seeded brain or a real Postgres version: the surfaces where gbrain master broke in the 30 days before 2026-11-09",
      "source": "eval/runner/nightly/smokes/ (built with the runner)",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "upgrade-from-previous",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "upgrade-from-old",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "ingest-retry-across-upgrade",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "managed-sync",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "source-pinned-sync",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "postgres-15",
          "role": "headroom"
        },
        {
          "id": "query-contract",
          "role": "headroom"
        }
      ],
      "note": "upgrade-from-previous: seeded brain written by the previous night's master, upgraded to tonight's; pages, writes, search, serve /health and /admin from an installed build. Fails at v0.60.553.0 over v0.60.552.0 (admin_bundle_missing), passes at v0.60.554.0 over v0.60.553.0. Its schema v265 pair counts as validated by its failure code: v0.60.465.0 over v0.60.390.0 fails with upgrade_migrations_failed, v0.60.466.0 over v0.60.390.0 passes the upgrade phase and then fails only on the separate /admin bug, and v0.60.554.0 over v0.60.390.0 passes; upgrade-from-old: seeded brain written by the old release v0.52.2.0 (the last release before managed persistence), upgraded with post-upgrade and the claim and activate runbook; a commit made after the upgrade becomes searchable while legacy pages wait (fails at v0.60.338.0 with legacy_sweep_blocks_commit; v0.60.339.0 passes that check and fails only the next) and a Git edit to a legacy page imports with no file_drift hold (fails at v0.60.370.0 with legacy_edit_held_file_drift, passes at v0.60.371.0); ingest-retry-across-upgrade: a POST /ingest capture accepted before the upgrade and retried after it never writes the old body over a newer edit. Fails at v0.60.609.0 over v0.60.608.0 (retry_overwrote_newer_edit), passes at v0.60.610.0 over v0.60.608.0; managed-sync: managed sync against a bare remote: hub index.md files with their own slug lines stay unheld (fail at v0.60.337.0 and v0.60.400.0 with hub_index_held, pass at v0.60.401.0), and a page delete whose first push is refused still reaches the remote (fails at v0.60.317.0 with delete_not_pushed, passes at v0.60.318.0); source-pinned-sync: a source rooted at its repository root under a source-root pin syncs without revision_conflict. Fails at v0.60.247.0 (checkpoint_revision_conflict), passes at v0.60.248.0; postgres-15: managed sync and eight concurrent writes on Postgres 15 beside the current Postgres. Fails at v0.60.325.0 (sync_checkpoint_failed, on Postgres 15 only), passes at v0.60.326.0; query-contract: query --limit N with no budget returns N rows on a brain whose pages carry Facts fences. Fails at v0.60.491.0 and v0.60.554.0 (query_limit_not_honored), passes at v0.60.555.0; dropped before the freeze: large-page-write-latency (writes to a page over 4 MiB while its search index builds), which on a Ubicloud VM passed at break releases between v0.60.331.0 and v0.60.335.0, before and after one respecification"
    },
